==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Kinrangers RoboForce''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Kinrangers GigaForce''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Like the other [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|ULTRA SOULS]], Kintaro has significantly different stats between Normal (spammable) and Evolved Form (high performance), both of which can be used effectively depending on the situation.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Kintaro does a very good job vs. Angel enemies being a spammable unit with good Slow chance and duration; a small stack of Kintaros is enough to perma-slow Angel enemies, even outranging nastier Angels like [[Boraphim]], [[Angelic Gory]] and [[Winged Pigge]].

For generalist purposes, Kintaro can be used alongside [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Vaulter Cat]] as they share similar stats.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Kinrangers RoboForce now outrange more Angel enemies, like [[Angelic Sleipnir]] and [[Chickful A]]. Similar to their previous form, they're very good at slowing these Angels too thanks to their three-part [[Multi-Hit]], which makes their chances of Slow ''87.5%'', combined with their high uptime.

Can be used as a generalist sniper with a very good 500 standing range, wide LD, and above-average DPS due to [[Savage Blow]]. Its high speed allows it to be deployed reactively, and it has enough backswing to mostly avoid clipping issues.

==='''True Form'''===
Kinrangers GigaForce gain higher health, damage and the Curse ability. The stat improvements are nice, but aren't so much of a change to justify their [[Catfruit]] costs. The Curse ability is an interesting one, as Angels don't have many debuffers, but is very effective against [[Angelic Sleipnir]], [[Winged Pigge]], [[Bears Be Back]] and [[Heavenly Herald Papuu]], which allows you to negate their main source of pushing power. However, it is not relevant for any other enemies and therefore, not a high priority given the difficulty of grinding two Elder Catfruits from [[Growing Strange]].

==='''Talents'''===
Kinrangers GigaForce's Talents are mediocre at best. Starting with the best of them, '''Target Red''' is only average, as a wide variety of consistent counters already exist in terms of brute force, and while slow does serve to paralyze them, Curse is redundant due to their general lack of meaningful abilities. Increasing their '''Curse''' duration would be helpful, but the small bonus isn't worth the massive NP cost. '''Resist Freeze''' is incredibly situational, as Curse can potentially shut it off before they are frozen, and they do have the range to avoid it, with outliers easily tackled by other units. '''Attack''' and '''HP Buff''' are obviously helpful, though using Catseyes on them before investing NP into these Talents is recommended.

